data: {"call_id":"call_Rp7srwTg6S5Kr9qOzPtrvbGo","results":[{"date":"2026-09-14","id":1,"last_updated":"2026-09-15","snippet":"Library to easily interface with LLM API providers\npip install litellm","source":"web","title":"litellm - PyPI","url":"https://pypi.org/project/litellm/"},{"date":"2026-03-24","id":2,"last_updated":"2026-08-25","snippet":"- The compromised PyPI packages were **litellm==1.82.7** and**litellm==1.82.8**.\nThose packages were live on March 24, 2026 from 10:39 UTC for about 40 minutes before being quarantined by PyPI.\n...\n- ~~We have paused all new LiteLLM releases until we complete a broader supply-chain review and confirm the release path is safe.~~**Updated:** We have now released a new**safe** version of LiteLLM (v1.83.0) by our new CI/CD v2 pipeline which added isolated environments, stronger security gates, and safer release separation for LiteLLM.\n...\nThe following LiteLLM versions published to PyPI were impacted:\n- **v1.82.7**: contained a malicious payload in the LiteLLM AI Gateway\n```\nproxy_server.py\n```\n- **v1.82.8**: contained\n```\nlitellm_init.pth\n```\nand a malicious payload in the LiteLLM AI Gateway\n```\nproxy_server.py\n```\nIf you installed or ran either of these versions, review the recommendations below immediately.\nNote: These versions have already been removed from PyPI.\n...\nYou may be affected if **any** of the following are true:\n- You installed or upgraded LiteLLM via\n```\npip\n```\non**March 24, 2026**, between**10:39 UTC and 16:00 UTC**\n- You ran\n...\npip install litellm\n```\nwithout pinning a version and received**v1.82.7** or**v1.82.8**\n- You built a Docker image during this window that included\n```\npip install litellm\n```\nwithout a pinned version\n- A dependency in your project pulled in LiteLLM as a transitive, unpinned dependency (for example through AI agent frameworks, MCP servers, or LLM orchestration tools)\n...\n### How to check if you are affected​\n- SDK\n- PROXY\n- GitHub Actions\n- GitLab CI\n```\npip show litellm\n```\nGo to the proxy base url, and check the version of the installed LiteLLM.\n...\npython find_litellm_github.py\n```\n...\nIf you installed or ran **v1.82.7** or **v1.82.8**, take the following actions immediately.\n### 1.\nRotate all secrets​\nTreat any credentials present on the affected systems as compromised, including:\n- API keys\n- Cloud access keys\n- Database passwords\n- SSH keys\n- Kubernetes tokens\n- Any secrets stored in environment variables or configuration files\n### 2.\nInspect your filesystem​\nCheck your\n...\n```\nfind /usr/lib/python3.13/site-packages/ -name \"litellm_init.pth\"\n```\nIf present:\n- remove it immediately\n- investigate the host for further compromise\n- preserve relevant artifacts if your security team is performing forensics\n### 3.\nAudit version history​\nReview your:\n- Local environments\n- CI/CD pipelines\n- Docker builds\n- Deployment logs\nConfirm whether **v1.82.7** or **v1.82.8** was installed anywhere.\nPin LiteLLM to a known safe version such as **v1.82.6 or earlier**, or to a later verified release once announced.\n...\nIf you believe your systems may be affected, contact us immediately:\n- **Security:**\n```\nsecurity@berri.ai\n```\n- **Support:**\n```\nsupport@berri.ai\n```\n- **Slack:** Reach out to the LiteLLM team directly","source":"web","title":"Security Update: Suspected Supply Chain Incident","url":"https://docs.litellm.ai/blog/security-update-march-2026"},{"date":"2026-08-14","id":3,"last_updated":"2026-08-18","snippet":"V balíčkovém indexu Pythonu, tedy na PyPI, má dnes 1 189 verzí a 2 915 souborů.\nKolik místa smí projekt na indexu zabrat, je ale omezené – a LiteLLM na to 11.\nsrpna 2026 narazil uprostřed vydávání verze 1.96.1.\n...\nNa indexu tak stojí verze, kterou tvoří čtyři instalační balíčky ve formátu wheel (koncovka\n```\n.whl\n```\n) pro Python 3.10 – pro macOS na Intelu, macOS na ARM a pro Linux s knihovnou glibc na aarch64 a x86-64.\nDohromady 104,6 MB.\n...\nPyPI hlídá dvě čísla: velikost jednoho souboru a součet všech souborů projektu.\nVýchozí meze jsou podle dokumentace indexu 100,0 MB na soubor a 10,0 GB na projekt.\n...\nSečtou-li se pole s velikostí u všech 2 915 souborů, které o projektu vypisuje JSON rozhraní PyPI, vyjde 26,56 GB.\n...\nVerze 1.96.2 vyšla 11.\nsrpna ve 21:12 UTC a má osm souborů: sedm wheelů a zdrojový archiv.\nSedm místo pětatřiceti proto, že jsou označené\n```\ncp310-abi3\n```\n. Zkratka abi3 znamená stabilní binární rozhraní Pythonu – knihovna z něj používá jen tu část, která se mezi verzemi jazyka nemění, takže jeden soubor platí pro Python 3.10 i pro všechny novější. Pět wheelů na platformu se tím smrskne na jeden.\nVydání kleslo z 933,6 MB na 186,2 MB, tedy o 80,1 % (podíl obou součtů). Ve velikosti 1.96.0 by se do výchozí desetigigabajtové kvóty vešlo necelých jedenáct vydání, ve velikosti 1.96.2 skoro čtyřiapadesát.\n...\nVerze proto na indexu zůstává tak, jak je: nestažená, bez zdrojového archivu a bez wheelů pro Python 3.11 až 3.14. Kdo si ji vyžádá jménem, nainstaluje ji jedině na Pythonu 3.10 a jen na čtyřech ze sedmi platforem; jinde není z čeho. Značka","source":"web","title":"LiteLLM vyčerpal místo na PyPI uprostřed vydávání | AI světem","url":"https://aisvetem.cz/litellm-pypi-kvota-ctyri-soubory-z-36-a105"},{"date":"2025-03-30","id":4,"last_updated":"2026-03-24","snippet":"Library to easily interface with LLM API providers\n## Project description\n...\nCall all LLM APIs using the OpenAI format [Bedrock, Huggingface, VertexAI, TogetherAI, Azure, OpenAI, Groq etc.]\n...\n\u003e LiteLLM v1.0.0 now requires `openai\u003e=1.0.0`.\n...\n\u003e LiteLLM v1.40.14+ now requires `pydantic\u003e=2.0.0`.\nNo changes required.\n```\npip install litellm\n```\n...\n```\npip install 'litellm[proxy]'\n```\n...\n|Provider|Completion|Streaming|Async Completion|Async Streaming|Async Embedding|Async Image Generation|","source":"web","title":"litellm-plus","url":"https://pypi.org/project/litellm-plus/"},{"date":"2026-09-16","id":5,"last_updated":"2026-09-19","snippet":"## Latest commit\ndependabot[bot]\nbuild(deps): bump anyio from 4.12.1 to 4.14.2 in the python-security …\nSep 18, 2026\nb18a57c · Sep 18, 2026\n## History\n...\n|.release-please-manifest.json|.release-please-manifest.json|.release-please-manifest.json|chore(main): release langchain-litellm 0.7.2 ( #269 )|Sep 16, 2026|\n...\nlangchain-litellm: v0.7.2Latest\nSep 16, 2026\n+ 25 releases","source":"web","title":"langchain-litellm - GitHub","url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langchain-litellm"},{"date":"2026-04-15","id":6,"last_updated":"2026-09-17","snippet":"pydantic-ai-litellm has been downloaded 163,580 times in total on PyPI, including 19,628 in the last 30 days.\nThe latest version is 0.2.5, released Apr 15, 2026.\nVersion0.2.5\nDownloads\n...\nUpdatedApr 15, 2026\nSource →PyPI →\nVersionsTotal0.*","source":"web","title":"pydantic-ai-litellm · 158.1k downloads on PyPI - pepy.tech","url":"https://pepy.tech/projects/pydantic-ai-litellm"},{"date":"2026-08-11","id":7,"last_updated":"2026-08-12","snippet":"All LiteLLM Docker images are signed with cosign.\nEvery release is signed with the same key introduced in commit `0112e53`.\n**Verify using the pinned commit hash (recommended):**\nA commit hash is cryptographically immutable, so this is the strongest way to ensure you are using the original signing key:\n```\ncosign verify \\\n--key https://raw.githubusercontent.com/BerriAI/litellm/0112e53046018d726492c814b3644b7d376029d0/cosign.pub \\\nghcr.io/berriai/litellm:v1.96.2\n```\n**Verify using the release tag (convenience):**\nTags are protected in this repository and resolve to the same key.\nThis option is easier to read but relies on tag protection rules:\n```\ncosign verify \\\n--key https://raw.githubusercontent.com/BerriAI/litellm/v1.96.2/cosign.pub \\\nghcr.io/berriai/litellm:v1.96.2\n```\nExpected output:\n...\nThe following checks were performed on each of these signatures:\n- The cosign claims were validated\n- The signatures were verified against the specified public key\n```\n...\n- chore(release): backport proxy request-handling maintenance and refresh runtime deps for 1.96.1 by @yuneng-berri in #36494\n- bump: version 1.96.1 → 1.96.2 (1.96.1 burned by the PyPI storage failure) by @yuneng-berri in #36570\n**Full Changelog**: v1.96.0...v1.96.2","source":"web","title":"BerriAI/litellm v1.96.2 on GitHub","url":"https://newreleases.io/project/github/BerriAI/litellm/release/v1.96.2"},{"date":"2026-09-16","id":8,"last_updated":"2026-09-19","snippet":"# langchain-litellm 0.7.2\n...\n## Data verified by PyPI on Sep 16, 2026\n## Key dates","source":"web","title":"langchain-litellm - PyPI","url":"https://pypi.org/project/langchain-litellm/"},{"date":"2026-08-11","id":9,"last_updated":"2026-08-15","snippet":"# litellm\n1.96.2\nlatest\n**Artifact:**\nlitellm-1.96.2-cp310-abi3-win_amd64.whl\nlatest\nTop 1k\nLibrary to easily interface with LLM API providers\n**License:** Permissive (MIT)\n**Published:** 3 days agoVisit GitHubSee on PyPI\n### SAFE Assessment","source":"web","title":"Versions - litellm - PyPI | ReversingLabs Spectra Assure Community","url":"https://secure.software/pypi/packages/litellm/versions"},{"date":"2026-06-20","id":10,"last_updated":"2026-07-10","snippet":"Today the four supported lines are **1.89.x, 1.88.x, 1.87.x, and 1.86.x**.\nEverything **1.85.x and earlier** has reached end of life and will no longer actively receive updates.\nThe window rolls forward: when 1.90.x ships, 1.86.x rolls out and the supported set becomes 1.90.x, 1.89.x, 1.88.x, and 1.87.x.\n...\n**Migration:**\n- **Rolling stable (Docker)** → `ghcr.io/berriai/litellm:latest`\n- **Reproducible pin (Docker)** → `ghcr.io/berriai/litellm:1.84.0`\n- **Reproducible pin (PyPI)** → `pip install litellm==1.84.0`","source":"web","title":"2 posts tagged with \"release\" - LiteLLM","url":"https://docs.litellm.ai/blog/tags/release"},{"id":11,"last_updated":"2026-09-18","snippet":"PyPI page\n...\nAuthor: BerriAI\nSummary: Library to easily interface with LLM API providers\nLatest version: 1.101.0","source":"web","title":"litellm","url":"https://pypistats.org/packages/litellm"},{"date":"2026-08-14","id":12,"last_updated":"2026-08-16","snippet":"### 2.\n安装（含两个坑）\n模型机没有 `python3-venv` 且不想动 sudo，用 `--without-pip` + get-pip 引导：\n```\npython3 -m venv --without-pip ~/deepseek-v4-flash/shim-venv\ncurl -sSL https://bootstrap.pypa.io/get-pip.py -o /tmp/get-pip.py\n~/deepseek-v4-flash/shim-venv/bin/python /tmp/get-pip.py -i https://pypi.tuna.tsinghua.edu.cn/simple\n~/deepseek-v4-flash/shim-venv/bin/pip install -i https://pypi.tuna.tsinghua.edu.cn/simple \\\n\"litellm[proxy]\" \"fastapi==0.115.12\" \"sse-starlette==2.2.1\"\n```\n**坑 1**：litellm 1.96.2 与最新 fastapi（0.141.x）不兼容——`litellm/proxy/management_endpoints/.../common.py` 引用了 fastapi 0.12x 移除的内部函数 `get_flat_dependant`，启动即 `ImportError`。锁 `fastapi==0.115.12` 解决。\n**坑 2**：锁了旧 fastapi 后 starlette 被拉到 0.46，而 sse-starlette 3.4.8 要求 starlette≥0.49——SSE 流式会埋雷。再锁 `sse-starlette==2.2.1` 对齐。\n...\nDS_API_KEY=$(cat .api-key) ./shim-venv/bin/litellm \\","source":"web","title":"一个模型同时讲OpenAI、Responses 和Anthropic 三种“方言“","url":"https://deepseek.csdn.net/6a7e933410ee7a33f29ad512.html"},{"date":"2026-03-27","id":13,"last_updated":"2026-08-26","snippet":"On March 24, 2026 at 10:39 UTC, LiteLLM v1.82.7 was pushed to PyPI.","source":"web","title":"Security Townhall Updates - LiteLLM Docs","url":"https://docs.litellm.ai/blog/security-townhall-updates"},{"date":"2026-09-17","id":14,"last_updated":"2026-09-19","snippet":"Published: 3 years ago Last updated: 1 days ago Latest version: 1.103.0.dev2\npip\n...\nBased on the latest version 1.101.0\nShow only direct vulnerabilities in latest version\n...\n|version|published|direct vulnerabilities|\n...\n|1.103.0.dev2|18 Sep, 2026|- 0 C - 1 H - 2 M - 0 L|","source":"web","title":"litellm - Snyk Security Database","url":"https://security.snyk.io/package/pip/litellm"},{"date":"2026-03-30","id":15,"last_updated":"2026-09-15","snippet":"On March 24, 2026, two malicious versions of LiteLLM were published to PyPI.\n...\n**What it is: ** Supply chain compromise of LiteLLM versions 1.82.7 and 1.82.8 on PyPI, injecting a three-stage credential stealer with Kubernetes lateral movement and persistent backdoor.\n...\n**Patch status: ** Both versions removed from PyPI.\nEntire litellm project quarantined pending review.\nLast known-clean version: litellm 1.82.6 (published March 22, 2026).\n...\n|Component|Vulnerable|Safe Version|Notes|\n...\n|litellm (PyPI)|1.82.7|1.82.6|Payload in proxy_server.py; import-time execution|\n|litellm (PyPI)|1.82.8|1.82.6|proxy_server.py + litellm_init.pth; fires on every Python startup|\n...\n1. Check installed version: pip show litellm 2\u003e/dev/null | grep Version\n2. Search for .pth file: find “$(python3 -c ‘import site; print(site.getsitepackages()[0])’)” -name “litellm_init.pth” 2\u003e/dev/null\n3. Check lock files: grep litellm requirements.txt poetry.lock uv.lock Pipfile.lock 2\u003e/dev/null\n4. Search for persistence: ls -la ~/.config/sysmon/sysmon.py ~/.config/systemd/user/sysmon.service /tmp/pglog /tmp/.pg_state 2\u003e/dev/null\n5. Check Kubernetes: kubectl get pods -n kube-system | grep node-setup\n6. Review network logs for connections to models.litellm[.]cloud and checkmarx[.]zone\n7. Check systemd: systemctl –user status sysmon.service 2\u003e/dev/null\n8. Audit BerriAI org packages: any package published through the same CI/CD infrastructure should be treated as suspect\n...\n1. Identify affected systems: pip show litellm | grep Version across all environments.\nCheck lock files for pinned 1.82.7 or 1.82.8.\n2. Uninstall immediately: pip uninstall litellm.\nRemove litellm_init.pth from site-packages.\n3. Kill persistence: systemctl –user stop sysmon.service \u0026\u0026 systemctl –user disable sysmon.service.\nRemove ~/.config/sysmon/ and ~/.config/systemd/user/sysmon.service.\nKill /tmp/pglog processes.\nRemove /tmp/pglog and /tmp/.pg_state.\n4. Block C2 at network/DNS: models.litellm[.]cloud and checkmarx[.]zone.\n...\nPin dependencies to exact versions and verify package integrity against the upstream source repository, not just the registry’s own RECORD hashes.\n...\nSource-to-artifact comparison is the only reliable detection method.\nEnable PyPI Trusted Publishers (OIDC-based publishing) to eliminate long-lived API tokens from CI pipelines.\nIf a pipeline does not need a PyPI token, do not give it one.\n...\nImplement a delay before adopting new package versions.","source":"web","title":"TeamPCP Attack day 6 Backdoors LiteLLM","url":"https://phoenix.security/teampcp-litellm-supply-chain-compromise-pypi-credential-stealer-kubernetes/"}],"sequence_number":6,"thought":"Found 15 results","type":"response.reasoning.search_results"}

event: response.output_item.done
data: {"item":{"queries":["PyPI litellm 1.96.2","litellm PyPI latest version"],"results":[{"date":"2026-09-14","id":1,"last_updated":"2026-09-15","snippet":"Library to easily interface with LLM API providers\npip install litellm","source":"web","title":"litellm - PyPI","url":"https://pypi.org/project/litellm/"},{"date":"2026-03-24","id":2,"last_updated":"2026-08-25","snippet":"- The compromised PyPI packages were **litellm==1.82.7** and**litellm==1.82.8**.\nThose packages were live on March 24, 2026 from 10:39 UTC for about 40 minutes before being quarantined by PyPI.\n...\n- ~~We have paused all new LiteLLM releases until we complete a broader supply-chain review and confirm the release path is safe.~~**Updated:** We have now released a new**safe** version of LiteLLM (v1.83.0) by our new CI/CD v2 pipeline which added isolated environments, stronger security gates, and safer release separation for LiteLLM.\n...\nThe following LiteLLM versions published to PyPI were impacted:\n- **v1.82.7**: contained a malicious payload in the LiteLLM AI Gateway\n```\nproxy_server.py\n```\n- **v1.82.8**: contained\n```\nlitellm_init.pth\n```\nand a malicious payload in the LiteLLM AI Gateway\n```\nproxy_server.py\n```\nIf you installed or ran either of these versions, review the recommendations below immediately.\nNote: These versions have already been removed from PyPI.\n...\nYou may be affected if **any** of the following are true:\n- You installed or upgraded LiteLLM via\n```\npip\n```\non**March 24, 2026**, between**10:39 UTC and 16:00 UTC**\n- You ran\n...\npip install litellm\n```\nwithout pinning a version and received**v1.82.7** or**v1.82.8**\n- You built a Docker image during this window that included\n```\npip install litellm\n```\nwithout a pinned version\n- A dependency in your project pulled in LiteLLM as a transitive, unpinned dependency (for example through AI agent frameworks, MCP servers, or LLM orchestration tools)\n...\n### How to check if you are affected​\n- SDK\n- PROXY\n- GitHub Actions\n- GitLab CI\n```\npip show litellm\n```\nGo to the proxy base url, and check the version of the installed LiteLLM.\n...\npython find_litellm_github.py\n```\n...\nIf you installed or ran **v1.82.7** or **v1.82.8**, take the following actions immediately.\n### 1.\nRotate all secrets​\nTreat any credentials present on the affected systems as compromised, including:\n- API keys\n- Cloud access keys\n- Database passwords\n- SSH keys\n- Kubernetes tokens\n- Any secrets stored in environment variables or configuration files\n### 2.\nInspect your filesystem​\nCheck your\n...\n```\nfind /usr/lib/python3.13/site-packages/ -name \"litellm_init.pth\"\n```\nIf present:\n- remove it immediately\n- investigate the host for further compromise\n- preserve relevant artifacts if your security team is performing forensics\n### 3.\nAudit version history​\nReview your:\n- Local environments\n- CI/CD pipelines\n- Docker builds\n- Deployment logs\nConfirm whether **v1.82.7** or **v1.82.8** was installed anywhere.\nPin LiteLLM to a known safe version such as **v1.82.6 or earlier**, or to a later verified release once announced.\n...\nIf you believe your systems may be affected, contact us immediately:\n- **Security:**\n```\nsecurity@berri.ai\n```\n- **Support:**\n```\nsupport@berri.ai\n```\n- **Slack:** Reach out to the LiteLLM team directly","source":"web","title":"Security Update: Suspected Supply Chain Incident","url":"https://docs.litellm.ai/blog/security-update-march-2026"},{"date":"2026-08-14","id":3,"last_updated":"2026-08-18","snippet":"V balíčkovém indexu Pythonu, tedy na PyPI, má dnes 1 189 verzí a 2 915 souborů.\nKolik místa smí projekt na indexu zabrat, je ale omezené – a LiteLLM na to 11.\nsrpna 2026 narazil uprostřed vydávání verze 1.96.1.\n...\nNa indexu tak stojí verze, kterou tvoří čtyři instalační balíčky ve formátu wheel (koncovka\n```\n.whl\n```\n) pro Python 3.10 – pro macOS na Intelu, macOS na ARM a pro Linux s knihovnou glibc na aarch64 a x86-64.\nDohromady 104,6 MB.\n...\nPyPI hlídá dvě čísla: velikost jednoho souboru a součet všech souborů projektu.\nVýchozí meze jsou podle dokumentace indexu 100,0 MB na soubor a 10,0 GB na projekt.\n...\nSečtou-li se pole s velikostí u všech 2 915 souborů, které o projektu vypisuje JSON rozhraní PyPI, vyjde 26,56 GB.\n...\nVerze 1.96.2 vyšla 11.\nsrpna ve 21:12 UTC a má osm souborů: sedm wheelů a zdrojový archiv.\nSedm místo pětatřiceti proto, že jsou označené\n```\ncp310-abi3\n```\n. Zkratka abi3 znamená stabilní binární rozhraní Pythonu – knihovna z něj používá jen tu část, která se mezi verzemi jazyka nemění, takže jeden soubor platí pro Python 3.10 i pro všechny novější. Pět wheelů na platformu se tím smrskne na jeden.\nVydání kleslo z 933,6 MB na 186,2 MB, tedy o 80,1 % (podíl obou součtů). Ve velikosti 1.96.0 by se do výchozí desetigigabajtové kvóty vešlo necelých jedenáct vydání, ve velikosti 1.96.2 skoro čtyřiapadesát.\n...\nVerze proto na indexu zůstává tak, jak je: nestažená, bez zdrojového archivu a bez wheelů pro Python 3.11 až 3.14. Kdo si ji vyžádá jménem, nainstaluje ji jedině na Pythonu 3.10 a jen na čtyřech ze sedmi platforem; jinde není z čeho. Značka","source":"web","title":"LiteLLM vyčerpal místo na PyPI uprostřed vydávání | AI světem","url":"https://aisvetem.cz/litellm-pypi-kvota-ctyri-soubory-z-36-a105"},{"date":"2025-03-30","id":4,"last_updated":"2026-03-24","snippet":"Library to easily interface with LLM API providers\n## Project description\n...\nCall all LLM APIs using the OpenAI format [Bedrock, Huggingface, VertexAI, TogetherAI, Azure, OpenAI, Groq etc.]\n...\n\u003e LiteLLM v1.0.0 now requires `openai\u003e=1.0.0`.\n...\n\u003e LiteLLM v1.40.14+ now requires `pydantic\u003e=2.0.0`.\nNo changes required.\n```\npip install litellm\n```\n...\n```\npip install 'litellm[proxy]'\n```\n...\n|Provider|Completion|Streaming|Async Completion|Async Streaming|Async Embedding|Async Image Generation|","source":"web","title":"litellm-plus","url":"https://pypi.org/project/litellm-plus/"},{"date":"2026-09-16","id":5,"last_updated":"2026-09-19","snippet":"## Latest commit\ndependabot[bot]\nbuild(deps): bump anyio from 4.12.1 to 4.14.2 in the python-security …\nSep 18, 2026\nb18a57c · Sep 18, 2026\n## History\n...\n|.release-please-manifest.json|.release-please-manifest.json|.release-please-manifest.json|chore(main): release langchain-litellm 0.7.2 ( #269 )|Sep 16, 2026|\n...\nlangchain-litellm: v0.7.2Latest\nSep 16, 2026\n+ 25 releases","source":"web","title":"langchain-litellm - GitHub","url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langchain-litellm"},{"date":"2026-04-15","id":6,"last_updated":"2026-09-17","snippet":"pydantic-ai-litellm has been downloaded 163,580 times in total on PyPI, including 19,628 in the last 30 days.\nThe latest version is 0.2.5, released Apr 15, 2026.\nVersion0.2.5\nDownloads\n...\nUpdatedApr 15, 2026\nSource →PyPI →\nVersionsTotal0.*","source":"web","title":"pydantic-ai-litellm · 158.1k downloads on PyPI - pepy.tech","url":"https://pepy.tech/projects/pydantic-ai-litellm"},{"date":"2026-08-11","id":7,"last_updated":"2026-08-12","snippet":"All LiteLLM Docker images are signed with cosign.\nEvery release is signed with the same key introduced in commit `0112e53`.\n**Verify using the pinned commit hash (recommended):**\nA commit hash is cryptographically immutable, so this is the strongest way to ensure you are using the original signing key:\n```\ncosign verify \\\n--key https://raw.githubusercontent.com/BerriAI/litellm/0112e53046018d726492c814b3644b7d376029d0/cosign.pub \\\nghcr.io/berriai/litellm:v1.96.2\n```\n**Verify using the release tag (convenience):**\nTags are protected in this repository and resolve to the same key.\nThis option is easier to read but relies on tag protection rules:\n```\ncosign verify \\\n--key https://raw.githubusercontent.com/BerriAI/litellm/v1.96.2/cosign.pub \\\nghcr.io/berriai/litellm:v1.96.2\n```\nExpected output:\n...\nThe following checks were performed on each of these signatures:\n- The cosign claims were validated\n- The signatures were verified against the specified public key\n```\n...\n- chore(release): backport proxy request-handling maintenance and refresh runtime deps for 1.96.1 by @yuneng-berri in #36494\n- bump: version 1.96.1 → 1.96.2 (1.96.1 burned by the PyPI storage failure) by @yuneng-berri in #36570\n**Full Changelog**: v1.96.0...v1.96.2","source":"web","title":"BerriAI/litellm v1.96.2 on GitHub","url":"https://newreleases.io/project/github/BerriAI/litellm/release/v1.96.2"},{"date":"2026-09-16","id":8,"last_updated":"2026-09-19","snippet":"# langchain-litellm 0.7.2\n...\n## Data verified by PyPI on Sep 16, 2026\n## Key dates","source":"web","title":"langchain-litellm - PyPI","url":"https://pypi.org/project/langchain-litellm/"},{"date":"2026-08-11","id":9,"last_updated":"2026-08-15","snippet":"# litellm\n1.96.2\nlatest\n**Artifact:**\nlitellm-1.96.2-cp310-abi3-win_amd64.whl\nlatest\nTop 1k\nLibrary to easily interface with LLM API providers\n**License:** Permissive (MIT)\n**Published:** 3 days agoVisit GitHubSee on PyPI\n### SAFE Assessment","source":"web","title":"Versions - litellm - PyPI | ReversingLabs Spectra Assure Community","url":"https://secure.software/pypi/packages/litellm/versions"},{"date":"2026-06-20","id":10,"last_updated":"2026-07-10","snippet":"Today the four supported lines are **1.89.x, 1.88.x, 1.87.x, and 1.86.x**.\nEverything **1.85.x and earlier** has reached end of life and will no longer actively receive updates.\nThe window rolls forward: when 1.90.x ships, 1.86.x rolls out and the supported set becomes 1.90.x, 1.89.x, 1.88.x, and 1.87.x.\n...\n**Migration:**\n- **Rolling stable (Docker)** → `ghcr.io/berriai/litellm:latest`\n- **Reproducible pin (Docker)** → `ghcr.io/berriai/litellm:1.84.0`\n- **Reproducible pin (PyPI)** → `pip install litellm==1.84.0`","source":"web","title":"2 posts tagged with \"release\" - LiteLLM","url":"https://docs.litellm.ai/blog/tags/release"},{"id":11,"last_updated":"2026-09-18","snippet":"PyPI page\n...\nAuthor: BerriAI\nSummary: Library to easily interface with LLM API providers\nLatest version: 1.101.0","source":"web","title":"litellm","url":"https://pypistats.org/packages/litellm"},{"date":"2026-08-14","id":12,"last_updated":"2026-08-16","snippet":"### 2.\n安装（含两个坑）\n模型机没有 `python3-venv` 且不想动 sudo，用 `--without-pip` + get-pip 引导：\n```\npython3 -m venv --without-pip ~/deepseek-v4-flash/shim-venv\ncurl -sSL https://bootstrap.pypa.io/get-pip.py -o /tmp/get-pip.py\n~/deepseek-v4-flash/shim-venv/bin/python /tmp/get-pip.py -i https://pypi.tuna.tsinghua.edu.cn/simple\n~/deepseek-v4-flash/shim-venv/bin/pip install -i https://pypi.tuna.tsinghua.edu.cn/simple \\\n\"litellm[proxy]\" \"fastapi==0.115.12\" \"sse-starlette==2.2.1\"\n```\n**坑 1**：litellm 1.96.2 与最新 fastapi（0.141.x）不兼容——`litellm/proxy/management_endpoints/.../common.py` 引用了 fastapi 0.12x 移除的内部函数 `get_flat_dependant`，启动即 `ImportError`。锁 `fastapi==0.115.12` 解决。\n**坑 2**：锁了旧 fastapi 后 starlette 被拉到 0.46，而 sse-starlette 3.4.8 要求 starlette≥0.49——SSE 流式会埋雷。再锁 `sse-starlette==2.2.1` 对齐。\n...\nDS_API_KEY=$(cat .api-key) ./shim-venv/bin/litellm \\","source":"web","title":"一个模型同时讲OpenAI、Responses 和Anthropic 三种“方言“","url":"https://deepseek.csdn.net/6a7e933410ee7a33f29ad512.html"},{"date":"2026-03-27","id":13,"last_updated":"2026-08-26","snippet":"On March 24, 2026 at 10:39 UTC, LiteLLM v1.82.7 was pushed to PyPI.","source":"web","title":"Security Townhall Updates - LiteLLM Docs","url":"https://docs.litellm.ai/blog/security-townhall-updates"},{"date":"2026-09-17","id":14,"last_updated":"2026-09-19","snippet":"Published: 3 years ago Last updated: 1 days ago Latest version: 1.103.0.dev2\npip\n...\nBased on the latest version 1.101.0\nShow only direct vulnerabilities in latest version\n...\n|version|published|direct vulnerabilities|\n...\n|1.103.0.dev2|18 Sep, 2026|- 0 C - 1 H - 2 M - 0 L|","source":"web","title":"litellm - Snyk Security Database","url":"https://security.snyk.io/package/pip/litellm"},{"date":"2026-03-30","id":15,"last_updated":"2026-09-15","snippet":"On March 24, 2026, two malicious versions of LiteLLM were published to PyPI.\n...\n**What it is: ** Supply chain compromise of LiteLLM versions 1.82.7 and 1.82.8 on PyPI, injecting a three-stage credential stealer with Kubernetes lateral movement and persistent backdoor.\n...\n**Patch status: ** Both versions removed from PyPI.\nEntire litellm project quarantined pending review.\nLast known-clean version: litellm 1.82.6 (published March 22, 2026).\n...\n|Component|Vulnerable|Safe Version|Notes|\n...\n|litellm (PyPI)|1.82.7|1.82.6|Payload in proxy_server.py; import-time execution|\n|litellm (PyPI)|1.82.8|1.82.6|proxy_server.py + litellm_init.pth; fires on every Python startup|\n...\n1. Check installed version: pip show litellm 2\u003e/dev/null | grep Version\n2. Search for .pth file: find “$(python3 -c ‘import site; print(site.getsitepackages()[0])’)” -name “litellm_init.pth” 2\u003e/dev/null\n3. Check lock files: grep litellm requirements.txt poetry.lock uv.lock Pipfile.lock 2\u003e/dev/null\n4. Search for persistence: ls -la ~/.config/sysmon/sysmon.py ~/.config/systemd/user/sysmon.service /tmp/pglog /tmp/.pg_state 2\u003e/dev/null\n5. Check Kubernetes: kubectl get pods -n kube-system | grep node-setup\n6. Review network logs for connections to models.litellm[.]cloud and checkmarx[.]zone\n7. Check systemd: systemctl –user status sysmon.service 2\u003e/dev/null\n8. Audit BerriAI org packages: any package published through the same CI/CD infrastructure should be treated as suspect\n...\n1. Identify affected systems: pip show litellm | grep Version across all environments.\nCheck lock files for pinned 1.82.7 or 1.82.8.\n2. Uninstall immediately: pip uninstall litellm.\nRemove litellm_init.pth from site-packages.\n3. Kill persistence: systemctl –user stop sysmon.service \u0026\u0026 systemctl –user disable sysmon.service.\nRemove ~/.config/sysmon/ and ~/.config/systemd/user/sysmon.service.\nKill /tmp/pglog processes.\nRemove /tmp/pglog and /tmp/.pg_state.\n4. Block C2 at network/DNS: models.litellm[.]cloud and checkmarx[.]zone.\n...\nPin dependencies to exact versions and verify package integrity against the upstream source repository, not just the registry’s own RECORD hashes.\n...\nSource-to-artifact comparison is the only reliable detection method.\nEnable PyPI Trusted Publishers (OIDC-based publishing) to eliminate long-lived API tokens from CI pipelines.\nIf a pipeline does not need a PyPI token, do not give it one.\n...\nImplement a delay before adopting new package versions.","source":"web","title":"TeamPCP Attack day 6 Backdoors LiteLLM","url":"https://phoenix.security/teampcp-litellm-supply-chain-compromise-pypi-credential-stealer-kubernetes/"}],"type":"search_results"},"output_index":0,"sequence_number":7,"type":"response.output_item.done"}

